-- title:
--   Kernel of the geometric fibre comparison is the invertible ideal (varpi)
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$, a nonzero natural number $M$ with $5 \le M$ and $p \nmid M$, a field $L$ of characteristic zero that is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of type $\{p\}$, and a primitive $p$-th root of unity $\zeta \in L$. Let $K$ be the intermediate field of $L \subseteq L((q))$ obtained by adjoining to $L$ the coefficientwise image of the function field $\mathrm{x1FunctionField}(Mp)$ of $X_1(Mp)$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ inside $\mathbb{Q}((q))$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$ such that $p$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$ and $\zeta$ is in the image of $A$, with a compatible $A$-algebra structure on $K$, and let $j \in K$ be nonzero with image the coefficientwise embedding of the $q$-expansion $\mathrm{jq}$. Let $k$ be an algebraically closed $A$-algebra field of characteristic $p$, write $X$ for the two-chart model [`ModularCurve.TwoChart.modelTo A K j`](def/ModularCurve_TwoChartModel.html#L252) over $\operatorname{Spec} A$, and let $C_1, C_2$ be proper, smooth of relative dimension $1$, geometrically integral schemes over $\operatorname{Spec} k$ together with closed immersions $i_1, i_2$ into the base change $X \times_A k$ over $\operatorname{Spec} k$, whose images cover every point of $X \times_A k$, such that $C_1 \times_{X \times_A k} C_2$ is reduced with cardinality $n > 0$. Let $O$ be a discrete valuation domain, $\rho_O : A \to O$ a ring map carrying the maximal ideal of $A$ onto that of $O$, and $\mathrm{to}\kappa : O \to k$ a ring map with $\mathrm{to}\kappa \circ \rho_O =$ the structure map $A \to k$. Finally let $bc : X \times_A k \to X \times_A O$ be a morphism commuting with the projections to $X$ and compatible with $\operatorname{Spec}(\mathrm{to}\kappa)$ on the base factors. The conclusion is threefold: the kernel ideal sheaf of $bc$ equals the pullback (comap) along the structure morphism $X \times_A O \to \operatorname{Spec} O$ of the kernel ideal sheaf of $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the residue map $O \to O/\mathfrak{m}_O$; this ideal sheaf is invertible in the sense that each point of $X \times_A O$ has an affine open neighbourhood of the form $X_f$ on which the ideal is generated by a single non-zero-divisor; and the dual of the module associated with this ideal sheaf is isomorphic to the monoidal unit of the category of modules on $X \times_A O$.
--
--   This identifies the ideal sheaf cutting out the special fibre of the $O$-model of the two-chart model of $X_1(Mp)$ as the principal, invertible ideal generated by a uniformiser, with trivial associated line bundle. It is used in the subsequent analysis of the degeneration of $X_1(Mp)$ at $p$, where the triviality of this vertical divisor class is needed to compare line bundles on the geometric special fibre with line bundles over $O$.
